.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:379:## Amendment — 2026-04-24 — `source_asof` population semantics + `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:383:The 2026-04-24 Claim Anatomy Review (`.docs/plans/claim-anatomy-review-2026-04-24.md` §10) identified that `source_asof: Option<DateTime<Utc>>` exists in §4 above as optional metadata but no code path actually populates it. Today's storage path stamps `observed_at = now` (`glean_provider.rs:1182`) regardless of when the underlying source was authored. The Glean/PTY prompts ask for `sourcedAt` per item (`dimension_prompts.rs:608`) but the returned timestamp lives in a JSON blob and is never lifted into the first-class column.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:391:`source_asof` is amended from "optional metadata" to **must-be-populated-when-knowable**, with an explicit population chain:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:394:populate(source_asof) = pick first available:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:395:  1. LLM-returned `sourcedAt` from `itemSource.sourcedAt` (per dimension_prompts.rs:608 contract)
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:401:If all four fail, `source_asof = None` AND the Provenance envelope emits a new warning variant:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:427:freshness_input_age = match (source_asof, observed_at):
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:437:The builder lifts `itemSource.sourcedAt` (when present in LLM output) and Glean document timestamps into `source_asof` automatically. Authors do not manually populate the field. The builder emits `SourceTimestampUnknown` when the population chain falls to step 4.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:443:| DOS-211 (Provenance Builder, spine) | Builder lifts `sourcedAt` from `itemSource` JSON or Glean document metadata into `source_asof`. Emits `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning on full fallback. |
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:446:| DOS-218 / DOS-219 (pilot abilities, spine) | Acceptance criteria include: produces ≥1 claim with `source_asof` populated and ≥1 claim with `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning, demonstrating the chain works both ways. |
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:447:| `glean_provider.rs:1182` write path | Lift Glean document timestamps into `source_asof` before writing SignalEvent / claim row. Don't stamp `observed_at = now` as the only timestamp. |
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:450:### E. Backfill from existing `ItemSource.sourced_at` (corrected 2026-04-24 PM per Codex finding 3)
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:452:The earlier draft of this amendment said "Backfill of historical claims is a non-goal; `source_asof` stays NULL on pre-amendment rows." **That was wrong.** Adversarial review surfaced that the existing `ItemSource.sourced_at` field in stored `intelligence.json` blobs IS the evidence-time timestamp, and is consumed today by suppression (`is_suppressed`) and timeliness logic (`services/accounts.rs:1253-1274`). Treating migrated claims as unknown-timestamp would apply `STALENESS_PADDING` to data whose timestamp is actually knowable — that's a regression dressed as conservatism.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:457:backfill source_asof for each migrated claim:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:458:  1. If the source IntelligenceJson item has `itemSource.sourcedAt` populated (parseable RFC3339 / ISO8601):
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:459:     → source_asof = parsed timestamp
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:460:  2. If the item has no itemSource (legacy items pre-ItemSource introduction):
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:461:     → source_asof = None AND emit ProvenanceWarning::SourceTimestampUnknown { fallback: ObservedAt }
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:462:  3. If itemSource.sourcedAt is malformed / future-dated / timezone-less:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:472:The migration applies these bounds to every parsed `source_asof`:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:483:  - timestamp > now + 30 days (near-future; legitimate for renewal dates but suspicious for source_asof)
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:498:- Auto-classifier for inferring `source_asof` from claim_text content (v1.5.x+).
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:499:- Backfill of `source_asof` from sources OTHER than existing `ItemSource.sourced_at` (e.g., re-fetching Glean documents to recover their timestamps for old claims). This is post-spine cleanup if needed.
