   138	### 6. Input and Output Contracts
   139	
   140	Every ability declares typed input and output structs in its own module. The output is always wrapped in `AbilityOutput<T>`, which carries provenance exactly once — the domain output does not re-embed it.
   141	
   142	```rust
   143	#[derive(Deserialize, Serialize, JsonSchema)]
   144	pub struct PrepareMeetingInput {
   145	    pub meeting_id: MeetingId,
   146	    pub depth: ContextDepth,              // Shallow | Standard | Deep
   147	    pub include_open_loops: bool,
   148	    pub schema_version: SchemaVersion,    // Required; no implicit LATEST for external callers
   149	}
   150	
   151	#[derive(Serialize, JsonSchema)]
   152	pub struct MeetingBrief {
   153	    pub meeting: MeetingSummary,
   154	    pub topics: Vec<Topic>,
   155	    pub attendee_context: Vec<AttendeeContext>,
   156	    pub open_loops: Vec<OpenLoop>,
   157	    pub what_changed_since_last: Vec<ChangeMarker>,
   158	    pub suggested_outcomes: Vec<SuggestedOutcome>,
   159	    pub schema_version: SchemaVersion,
   160	    // Note: no `provenance` field here. It lives in the AbilityOutput<T> wrapper below.
   161	}
   162	
   163	// The actual return type from prepare_meeting:
   164	pub type Output = AbilityOutput<MeetingBrief>;
   165	
   166	pub struct AbilityOutput<T> {
   167	    pub data: T,
   168	    pub provenance: Provenance,           // Canonical location — see ADR-0105
   169	    pub ability_version: AbilityVersion,  // Which version of the ability produced this
   170	    pub diagnostics: Diagnostics,         // Non-fatal warnings, missing sources, etc.
   171	}
   172	```
   173	
   174	Rules:
   175	
   176	- Provenance lives on `AbilityOutput<T>`, exactly one place. Domain output types never re-declare a `provenance` field. Reviewers reject such declarations at registration.
   177	- Field-level provenance attribution (how `suggested_outcomes[0]` ties back to specific signals) is specified in [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md). This ADR requires that the mechanism exist; 0105 defines the shape.
   178	- Inputs are versioned via `SchemaVersion` (newtype wrapping `u32`). External callers (MCP, future REST) MUST declare `schema_version`; no implicit latest. Internal callers (Tauri commands) may default to current since they rebuild with the ability. Versioning rules in §8.
   179	- Outputs are JSON-serializable via `serde` and expose a JSON Schema via `schemars` for external introspection. No trait objects, no opaque handles. This makes Tauri bridge, MCP tool registration, and docs generation all derive from the same schema source.
