## 8. Failure modes + rollback

Missing attribution, invalid subject fit, invalid composition refs, or bad declared confidence are hard finalize errors and return no `AbilityOutput<T>`. Unknown source timestamps are not hard errors; they produce `SourceTimestampUnknown` warnings per ADR-0105 (`.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:401-420`). Oversized provenance degrades by eliding deepest children; if still over 1MB, finalize fails so a raw oversize tree never leaves the ability.

